{"title":"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The midpoints of the sides of a regular hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> are joined to form a smaller hexagon. What fraction of the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> is enclosed by the smaller hexagon? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66664d57ff464bea26c246e5fa7e1f2fa9f9bbea.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(120); draw(rotate(30)*polygon(6)); draw(scale(2/sqrt(3))*polygon(6)); pair A=2/sqrt(3)*dir(120), B=2/sqrt(3)*dir(180), C=2/sqrt(3)*dir(240), D=2/sqrt(3)*dir(300), E=2/sqrt(3)*dir(0), F=2/sqrt(3)*dir(60); dot(A^^B^^C^^D^^E^^F); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, dir(origin--A)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, dir(origin--B)); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, dir(origin--C)); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, dir(origin--D)); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, dir(origin--E)); label(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, dir(origin--F)); [/asy]\" width=\"202\" height=\"175\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/1/ca1bddb7f65dfb91f7ff85516aaa49d07d7d779c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\qquad\\text{(B)}\\ \\frac{\\sqrt 3}{3}\\qquad\\text{(C)}\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\qquad\\text{(D)}\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\qquad\\text{(E)}\\ \\frac{\\sqrt 3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"379\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/b/49b0eb32dcd013f9e19f15a836fe29b46e63fc34.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(120); draw(rotate(30)*polygon(6)); draw(scale(2/sqrt(3))*polygon(6)); pair A=2/sqrt(3)*dir(120), B=2/sqrt(3)*dir(180), C=2/sqrt(3)*dir(240), D=2/sqrt(3)*dir(300), E=2/sqrt(3)*dir(0), F=2/sqrt(3)*dir(60); pair O=(0,0); dot(A^^B^^C^^D^^E^^F^^O); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, dir(origin--A)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, dir(origin--B)); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, dir(origin--C)); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, dir(origin--D)); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, dir(origin--E)); label(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, dir(origin--F)); label(&quot;$O$&quot;, O, N); draw(O--D--C--cycle); [/asy]\" width=\"202\" height=\"175\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b314163f3d7b82d78944283deda01130ab862d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OCD$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is copied six times to form the hexagon, so if we find the ratio of the area of the kite inside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b314163f3d7b82d78944283deda01130ab862d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OCD$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> to the the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b314163f3d7b82d78944283deda01130ab862d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OCD$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> itself, it will be the same ratio.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbc9faf21cb7bf06b7a4859ae24436f0006367e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC=CD=OD =2$\" width=\"169\" height=\"12\" /> so that the area of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/e/d2e36b9c2d744465d8546777c7195093f91b7fc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}s^2}{4} = \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b314163f3d7b82d78944283deda01130ab862d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OCD$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is made up of a kite and two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c78b85058ee5e17f88e2cde302e48aad826b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> triangles.  The two hypotenuses of these two triangles form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, so the hypotenuse of each triangle must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a1e5624456f4383802751ad1341ba230db07c54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{2} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"45\" height=\"37\" />.  Thus, the legs of each triangle are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9191a5007067cff8f6d73f4d3419e08238f00b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" />, and the area of two of these triangles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1819d3882f38b1af04a873c9cbd5d442cb1ee1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Subtracting the area of the two triangles from the area of the equilateral triangle, we find that the area of the kite is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/1/6d1243863a5746c060a836a6a93733813d708913.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3} - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} = \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"134\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the ratio of areas is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1150a17bf1b733cb666be84d920c71fc96bb3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" />, which is option <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bdade53f471aab49f63d1a734979cc0c636640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see six isosceles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/9/b49321cfaebf35e4772876df69aa74f60e3b0321.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120-30-30$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"107\" height=\"13\" /> triangles at the vertices of the large hexagon.  If we let the side of the larger hexagon be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we find that the two congruent sides of these triangles are both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.  By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Sines\" title=\"Law of Sines\">Law of Sines</a>, we find that the third side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c73d79a656b8ccd9544113e84ea4d8b8caa91a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}}{\\sin 30^\\circ} = \\frac{x}{\\sin 120^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"142\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9b40d589434dfa28f1cc28b33b5ab773760c23a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 = \\frac{x}{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"57\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/9/ec9e8c657a9e44ea115fcbf6286dd2e1eb38c39f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"61\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>This third side of the triangle is the length of the edge of the hexagon.  The ratio of the sides of the small hexagon to the large hexagon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9191a5007067cff8f6d73f4d3419e08238f00b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" />, since the large hexagon has a unit side.  The ratio of the areas is the square of the ratio of the sides, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1150a17bf1b733cb666be84d920c71fc96bb3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" />, or option <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bdade53f471aab49f63d1a734979cc0c636640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME\" title=\"1996 AHSME\">1996 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1996 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1996\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017163839\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.053 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 222/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2494/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 152/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6566/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.265      1 -total\n 57.96%    7.109      1 Template:AHSME_box\n 40.16%    4.925      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10109:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017163839 and revision id 86335. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}